WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
Jaime Lannister: I was never supposed&nbsp;
to be on the Kingsguard. Oh, as a boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.840
I dreamed of the white cloak like all boys. But&nbsp;
I was heir to Tywin Lannister, Hand of the King.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:16.640
If he forbade the tides, the waves would cease.
Then I was fifteen, and my father was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.840
congratulating me on my new knighthood&nbsp;
in the Red Keep. I wonder if that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.480
was the last time he was proud of me.
That night, there was a knock on my door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.040
and I'd opened it to find my sister Cersei&nbsp;
disguised as a simple serving girl. I hadn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:37.600
seen her since my father took her to court when&nbsp;
she was twelve. She had grown up. As had I.
&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:44.240
She told me that my father planned to marry me&nbsp;
off to Lysa Tully. But she could arrange for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.440
king to raise me to the Kingsguard so I could stay&nbsp;
in the city with her. All I had to do was agree.
&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.920
I made the obvious objections. Our family,&nbsp;
our father, Casterly Rock. Until she asked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.960
"Is it a rock you want, or me?"&nbsp;
Come morning, she had my consent.
&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.600
I would join the Kingsguard for her. I&nbsp;
would forswear my lands and title for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:16.240
her. I would forsake our family for her.
Soon, a royal raven commanded my father to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.920
present me to the King during the Great&nbsp;
Tourney at Harrenhal to say my vows.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:26.160
My father erupted in fury.
He could not object openly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.920
but he resigned the Handship and returned&nbsp;
to Casterly Rock, taking Cersei with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:38.000
Instead of being together, Cersei and I exchanged&nbsp;
places. Then, everything started to fall apart.
&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:44.480
At Harrenhal, King Aerys made a great show of&nbsp;
my investiture. I knelt before him in gleaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.560
armor and swore the oath of the Kingsguard.
Once Ser Gerold Hightower raised me up and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.560
put the white cloak on my shoulders, a roar went&nbsp;
up from the crowd. I admit, despite my father's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:02:00.720
anger, I was happy. And foolish.
That very night, Aerys soured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.960
commanding me to return to the Red Keep to&nbsp;
guard the queen and little Prince Viserys.
&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.840
SerGerold offered to take that duty himself so I&nbsp;
might compete in the tourney, but Aerys refused.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:17.040
"He'll win no glory here," the king said. "He's&nbsp;
mine now, not Tywin's. He'll serve as I see fit."
&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:23.520
That was when I understood. It was not my&nbsp;
skill or valor that had won me this honor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:30.240
The Mad King had chosen me to spite my&nbsp;
father and steal his heir. I wanted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:36.160
rip off the white cloak, but it was too late.
Bronn: Most boys dream of becoming a Kingsguard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.880
Rich boys from good families get the chance.&nbsp;
Smart boys stay at home and sing songs about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.160
them instead, opening purses and thighs, because&nbsp;
the Kingsguard isn't really good for much else.
&nbsp;

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.600
There was one Kingsguard (I forgot the&nbsp;
bastard's name) who swore an oath to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.800
dying Targaryen king to crown his daughter&nbsp;
after him. The very night that king died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:02.000
this Kingsguard crowned the king's son instead.
When an old man on the small council dared to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:08.320
protest, this honorable knight opened his throat.&nbsp;
The bastard died in the very civil war he started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.520
along with the old king's son,&nbsp;
daughter, and most of their dragons.
&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.360
And the Kingsguard? All that duty and honor and&nbsp;
not enough brains to figure out which Targaryen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.800
to give it to. Twin brothers even ended&nbsp;
up on opposite sides, died with tears on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:27.360
their cheeks as they cut each other down.
I suppose I should think that's tragic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.840
but stupid men do stupid things every&nbsp;
day and nobody cries over them.
&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.480
Prince Aemon the Dragonknight may be the&nbsp;
most famous Kingsguard who ever lived.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:43.680
How did he die? Defending Aegon the Unworthy from&nbsp;
the brothers of a man whom Aegon fed to his dogs.
&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.640
The man's crime? Sleeping with one of&nbsp;
the many mistresses Aegon wasn't using,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:55.520
and the man was one of Aegon's own Kingsguard.
Arthur Dayne, Gerold Hightower. Sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.160
if half the stories about them are true, they&nbsp;
could swing a sword better than most. Makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.520
their lives even more of a waste. Bodyguards to&nbsp;
the maddest king the Seven Kingdoms ever saw.
&nbsp;

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:13.280
Watching their king burn men alive. Standing guard&nbsp;
as their king r**** his queen. Hiding the Stark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:18.880
girl that Prince Rhaegar stole away, causing&nbsp;
a war that toppled their king. And all this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:24.720
without any gold or women to show for it.
Stupid buggers! The only one with any sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.520
was Jaime Lannister. When his father stormed&nbsp;
the city, he put a sword through the Mad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:35.120
King's back rather than die gloriously at&nbsp;
his post. He's still here. They are not.
&nbsp;

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.120
Even if the Kingsguard are the&nbsp;
greatest knights in the realm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:45.440
knights are just arses in armor. Riding whatever&nbsp;
horse their daddies gave 'em. Putting on a white&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:51.200
cloak does not make a man smarter of bolder.
It's just a pretty little curtain. Behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.480
it is the same pile of shii.
Petyr Baelish: What the King dreams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:05:02.800
the Hand of the King builds, or so say the&nbsp;
Kings, the Hands, and Lords who wish to be Hands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:10.080
The lowborn put it differently: "The King&nbsp;
eats, and the Hand takes the shii." The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.600
fact is most Kings hate ruling. We shouldn't&nbsp;
blame them, their only qualification is blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:19.840
so naturally, they're wary&nbsp;
of a seat made of blades.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.800
Far better to find other men to rule in their&nbsp;
stead. But how should a King select his Hand?
&nbsp;

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:33.280
Strength? As little more than a boy, Ser Criston&nbsp;
Cole replaced the legendary Ser RyamRedwyne on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:38.560
the Kingsguard and soon rose to Lord Commander.&nbsp;
But knights only know one way to settle disputes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:44.480
When Prince Aegon's father died, SerCriston slit&nbsp;
the throat of an advisor who objected to Aegon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:50.000
ascension over his aunt, the anointed heir.&nbsp;
His actions so pleased the new King, Aegon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.600
Second of His Name, that he appointed SerCriston&nbsp;
as his Hand in the ensuing civil war called the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:02.240
Dance of Dragons. Neither SerCriston nor the King&nbsp;
nor even the Targaryen dragons would survive it.
&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.360
Jaime Lannister: All boys dream of&nbsp;
becoming knights. The boys with talent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:12.400
dream of becoming Kingsguard. The boys&nbsp;
without talent, well, I wouldn't know.
&nbsp;

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:17.200
I remember the day the Lord Commander&nbsp;
wrote my name down in the White Book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:22.160
the official record of the Kingsguard. At&nbsp;
sixteen, the youngest member ever to join,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:26.880
knighted by Ser Arthur and Ser Barristan for&nbsp;
valor against the Kingswood Brotherhood.
&nbsp;

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:32.960
An outlaw had decided to try his luck against&nbsp;
a lowly squire. He was not using his head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:39.440
so I took it off him. Shortly afterwards, King&nbsp;
Aerys the Second, who hadn't yet earned the title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:45.600
of the Mad King, took me into his service.
If I have ever been happy, it was that day.
&nbsp;

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:52.560
For centuries, the Kingsguard have been the glory&nbsp;
of the realm. Aegon the Conqueror had established&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:58.160
the order as his personal guardians after uniting&nbsp;
Westeros with fire and blood. He knew that some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.120
his subjects wouldn't take to conquest, and his&nbsp;
dragons were no use against knives in the dark.
&nbsp;

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:07.440
No doubt surrounding himself with the&nbsp;
greatest knights in Westeros made his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.080
rule more palatable and less foreign as well.
&nbsp;

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:15.680
Everyone in his kingdoms soon knew the names&nbsp;
and some of the songs of the Kingsguard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:20.960
I certainly did from earliest days.
Lord Commander Gerold Hightower, the White&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:28.480
Bull; Arthur Dayne, the Sword of the Morning;&nbsp;
Barristan Selmy, the Bold; Prince Lewyn Martell;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:35.200
OswellWhent; Jonothor Darry. And,&nbsp;
soon enough, the boy prodigy. Me.
&nbsp;

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:41.120
We protected the king and his family. We&nbsp;
killed his enemies and led his armies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:46.400
We gave him counsel when asked and kept his&nbsp;
secrets when not. We swore to hold no lands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:52.080
take no wives, and father no children. Like the&nbsp;
Night's Watch, except with a real job to do.
&nbsp;

00:07:53.120 --> 00:08:00.000
Was I awed to see my name inscribed in the&nbsp;
same book as my heroes? Of course not. I was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:07.440
sixteen and brilliant. I knew I belonged there.
Beside the name of Prince Aemon the Dragonknight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:13.200
who wielded the Valyrian sword Dark Sister.&nbsp;
He died defending King Aegon the Unworthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.880
from assassins, though the king had&nbsp;
insulted Aemon throughout his reign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:21.920
and had well earned his fate because&nbsp;
Prince Aemon had sworn our oath.
&nbsp;

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:28.560
Beside the name of Ser GwayneCorbray, who dueled&nbsp;
the Targaryen bastard Daemon Blackfyre for an hour&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:33.680
during the Battle of Redgrass Field though&nbsp;
outmatched and grievously wounded, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:39.440
SerGwayne had sworn our oath.
Beside the name of Ser Duncan the Tall, who,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:44.080
as a hedge knight, broke several of Prince Aerion&nbsp;
Targaryen's teeth while defending a Dornish woman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:48.640
He later rose to Lord Commander and&nbsp;
burned beside his King at Summerhall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:56.880
because Ser Duncan had sworn our oath.
And now, below the name of Jaime Lannister. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:06.800
know how it reads. What I did, even though I had&nbsp;
sworn our oath. That was years, and a hand ago.
&nbsp;

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:14.480
When I joined the Kingsguard, I fought beside&nbsp;
legends in the flesh. Their kind is dust now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:22.320
And the men who have taken their place?
Mud.Ser Boros Blount, the Fat. Ser Meryn Trant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.640
the Forgettable. Sandor Clegane,&nbsp;
the Dog Who Tucked Tail and Ran.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:33.440
Like mud, their names have soiled the&nbsp;
White Book, almost as much as mine.
&nbsp;

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.720
Varys: When Aegon returned to King's&nbsp;
Landing, he found assassins waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:43.280
for him in the streets of his own capital.
If not for Visenya, the Conqueror would not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:48.400
have enjoyed his conquest for very long.&nbsp;
From then on, the king and his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.400 --> 00:10:03.840
would be guarded by the seven greatest&nbsp;
knights in the realm: the Kingsguard.

